          "slide_id": "article-opening",
          "part_kind": "opening",
          "title": "The short version",
          "blocks": [
            { "kind": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                "Pay is changing on 1 October. Instead of one payment a month, you'll be paid twice — on the 15th and on the last working day.",
                "Your total annual pay is not changing. The same amount arrives across two dates instead of one."
              ],
              "sources": ["brief:key_messages.M1", "brief:key_messages.M2"] }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },

    {
      "section_id": "why-now",
      "title": "Why we're doing this",
      "order": 3,
      "message_ids": ["M3"],
      "audience_ids": ["A1"],
      "slides": [
        {
          "slide_id": "article-why",
          "part_kind": "whats-changing",
          "title": "Why we're doing this",
          "blocks": [
            { "kind": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                "You asked for it. More frequent pay was the single most requested change in each of our last two engagement surveys — most people find two dates easier to budget around than one.",
                "There's a second reason. The payroll system we run today loses vendor support in March 2027. We'd have had to move anyway, so we're making both changes at once rather than disrupting everyone twice in a year."
              ],
              "sources": ["brief:change.rationale", "brief:key_messages.M3"] }
          ]
        },
        {
          "slide_id": "article-quote",
          "part_kind": "pull-quote",
          "title": "Pull quote",
          "blocks": [
            { "kind": "text",
              "content": "More frequent pay was the top request in our last two engagement surveys.",
              "sources": ["brief:key_messages.M3"] }
          ]
        }
      ]
